    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d679">

                <pb facs="0715" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50A/153: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-21T18:00:00-04:00">September 21,
                            1939—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>177. Your 530 [<hi rendition="#italic">531</hi>], September 19, 9 a.m., fourth
                    sentence. You understand of course that, as stated in Hamilton’s letter of July
                        27,<anchor n="99" xml:id="d679-f1"/> the Americans in question have no
                    official status vis-à-vis this Government.</p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking only.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
